wg
Usage: wg [show|showconf|set|setconf|genkey|pubkey|genpsk] ...

Configure a wireguard interface -- the encrypted tunnel vos dials out
through, so it never has to listen on a network it does not trust.

	show [IFACE]		current state: peers, endpoints, handshakes
	showconf IFACE		the config, in a form you can save
	set IFACE ...		change keys, peers, endpoints at runtime
	setconf IFACE FILE	apply a whole config file
	genkey			make a new private key (to stdout)
	pubkey			read a private key on stdin, print its public key
	genpsk			make a pre-shared key

	wg genkey | tee private.key | wg pubkey > public.key
	wg set wg0 private-key private.key
	wg set wg0 peer PUBKEY endpoint HOST:PORT allowed-ips 10.9.0.0/24
	wg show

The interface itself is made and addressed with ip:
	ip link add wg0 type wireguard
	ip addr add 10.9.0.2/24 dev wg0
	ip link set wg0 up

wireguard roams: it survives the underlying address changing and resumes
a dropped link rather than resetting it, which is half of why a dropped
ssh session over it can be picked back up.

See also: ip, dropbear, dbclient
